<newsitem itemid="495588" id="root" date="1997-04-08" xml:lang="en">
<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank 96 own-a/c trading profits ease.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank 96 own-a/c trading profits ease.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    1,859   vs 1,446</p>
<p>    Group net profit			    1,214   vs 979</p>
<p>    Group pretax profit			 1,795   vs 1,193</p>
<p>    Group loan loss provisions		1,216   vs 886</p>
<p>    Net income per share			2.97    vs 2.39 dmk</p>
<p>    DVFA result per share		     2.98    vs 2.35 dmk</p>
<p>    Taxes					   581     vs 214</p>
<p>Balance on financial investments and</p>
<p>    extraordinary account		     -64     vs -253</p>
<p>    Group income from own-account trading 450     vs 455</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 5,974   vs 5,216</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     2,286   vs 1,922</p>
<p>    Other operating income		    379     vs 275</p>
<p>    Return on equity			    10.1    vs 9.3 pct</p>
<p>    Personnel expenses			  3,526   vs 3,286</p>
<p>    Other administrative expenses	   2,136   vs 2,043</p>
<p>    Other operating expenses		  352     vs 207</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total		 448,003 vs 404,167</p>
<p>    Dividend					1.35    vs 1.35 marks</p>
<p>    Group lending				 309,458 vs 260,273</p>
<p>    Liable funds				  23,504  vs 21,207</p>
<p>    Branches					1,045   vs 1,060</p>
<p>    Staff					   29,334  vs 29,615</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Commerzbank AG. The bank already reported net profit, operating profit and pre-tax profit on Monday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
